---
title: "Articles — NetAgents"
description: "Essays on agentic AI in networking: the protocol layer, the security model, and the road from scripted automation to autonomous networks. Community write-ups welcome."
navCurrent: articles
wideFooter: true
---
{% extends "base.njk" %}

{% block railnote %}Yours or a contributor's &mdash; see how to <a href="/about/#contribute">pitch one</a>.{% endblock %}

{% block head_extra %}
<link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="NetAgents articles" href="/feed.xml">
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap wrap-wide">
    <span class="eyebrow">Articles</span>
    <h1>Essays on agentic AI in networking</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="max-width: 62ch;">Longer pieces than the directory entries allow for: how the protocol layer works, what changes about security, and how far along the industry is. <a href="/feed.xml">RSS available</a> if you'd rather follow along that way.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="wrap wrap-wide">
<section class="entry-group">
  <div class="entry-grid">
    {% for post in collections.articles %}
    <article class="entry">
      <div class="entry-top">
        <span class="entry-id">{{ post.data.date | readableDate }}</span>
        {% if "community" in post.data.tags %}<span class="pill status-active">community</span>{% endif %}
      </div>
      <h3><a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.heading }}</a></h3>
      <p class="desc">{{ post.data.summary }}</p>
      <div class="entry-foot">
        <span class="pill">{{ post.data.tags | join(" · ") }}</span>
        <a class="entry-link" href="{{ post.url }}">read →</a>
      </div>
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
</div>
{% endblock %}
